# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in the system config, so a file
# written with LF endings makes every later git command print
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it".
#
# That is not only noise. Chromatic shells out to git to build its changed-file
# list for TurboSnap, and the warnings were captured into that list alongside
# real paths (see build 13). Pinning the rule here also makes checkouts
# identical on Windows, macOS, Linux and CI instead of depending on each
# developer's global git config.
#
# The index is already LF for every text file, so this normalises working trees
# without changing any committed content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by end-of-line conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
